From 9d5ce0b8780b0d9a2e56ced1ec085e38e0daea0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:38:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] feat(agents): the Agent platform is a preview behind
 AGENTS_PLATFORM_ENABLED (default off)

Plan step 4.5 asked for a decision per dormant subsystem: wire it with a
date, delete it, or put it behind a flag labelled as future work. This
takes the third option for the whole platform (agents, knowledge bases,
tool registry, evaluations, governance, document ACL) so the product
decision can be made subsystem by subsystem later without dead routes
being reachable in the meantime:

- `agents_platform_enabled` (env AGENTS_PLATFORM_ENABLED, default false).
- app.main mounts the five agent routers only when it is on; otherwise
  /api/agents and /api/admin/{agents,knowledge,...} do not exist (404).
- preflight_stream_chat refuses a chat body that carries agent fields with
  400 when the flag is off, so the proxy never enters the agent path.
- /api/auth/session gains `features: {"agents_platform": bool}`; the admin
  navigation filters preview menus from that flag (and blocks direct
  /admin/agents... navigation), and the section is titled
  "Agents & Knowledge (preview)" when on. The chat agent picker already
  degrades to nothing when the catalog request fails.
- The knowledge_scheduler compose service is unchanged: its workers are
  idle without documents and keep the data plane consistent for installs
  that turn the flag on.

The import coupling inside proxy_service (agent request parsing, runtime
errors) stays because the chat path legitimately consumes the platform
when it is enabled; it is now a single guarded entry point.

Tests: flag default, routers absent, session flag, preflight refusal.
1375 tests; frontend tsc/eslint/vitest/knip clean.

